A||||12||Shiner||Emissions Test Fail, Suggestions?!?||||9||
Z||000000||Shiner||09-28-2001||04:58 PM||||Well, after all the paint and bodywork, the car failed PA emmissions as well as inspection  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <P>Engine is a 2.8.  The CO was .91, which is .3 over, and NOX was 2157 (should be under 1184)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  What do you guys think is the culprit here? And for some reason, it is listed as an 89 on the emissions, but an '87 on the registration?!? <P>After all this time, work, and $$$, this is really disapointing.  <P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||9
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||09-28-2001||06:14 PM||||Out here in California, when Im up for a smog, I install a brand new 02 sensor (I prefer Delco) the day of the test. If that doesn't pass me, and its only failed me once so far, I get a new cat for it.<P>The 02 sensor is probably the easiest thing to do first. <P>Good luck!||||reg||6
Z||000002||72vinman||09-28-2001||06:17 PM||||That's exactly what happened to me. I replaced the O2 with a new Bosch sensor and passed second time around. The CO level the 2nd time was .01 with the new sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||09-28-2001||06:19 PM||||High NOx can also be caused by a leak in the EGR tube or the EGR itself. With the engine cool you can remove the EGR and clean the holes/valves in the bottom. (Usually carboned up) Also spray out the throttle body with cleaner too. Check for vacuum leaks and also putting in a fresh set of good plugs could help too. If the above doesn't work than try the O2 and/or the Catalytic Converter.<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">      <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||GarethWright||09-29-2001||03:37 AM||||Man oh Man, isnt Oklahoma great! No State Inspections Anymore (Die Planet!) And back (3 months ago) when we did, if you fail, go down the street and take it again.  Downside is that theres a new tax when you buy the car (lucky me, I missed that one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<BR>but other than that, yea o2, maybe lower octane gasoline? (no idea, might work) spark plugs?||||reg||1
